  "result": "I added `parseRange` in `src/core/range.ts` and committed it. `npm run fast` passes (Biome, boundaries, tsc and 18 related tests).\n\n- **Behaviour:** `parseRange('1-3,5')` returns `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. It accepts single numbers and spaces around them. It throws on malformed segments (such as `a` or an empty entry) and on descending ranges like `3-1`.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/range.test.ts` uses `node:test` and covers expansion, single numbers with spaces, and the error cases. I added a weight for it in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **No helpers reused:** `src/core` can only import from itself, and `src/core/index.ts` has no helpers to reuse. Importing from the other `src/` areas would break the core boundary check.\n- **No task id in the commit title:** The conventions want the task id at the end of the title, but none was given in the brief, so the title is \"Add parseRange to expand numeric range lists\". If you give me the id, I can amend the title.",
